{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/457744-homebrew-stygian-lineage-void-filled-and-crazy","id":457744,"title":"[Homebrew] Stygian Lineage: Void-filled and Crazy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-25T21:36:20-07:00","id":457744,"title":"[Homebrew] Stygian Lineage: Void-filled and Crazy","content":"Hello everyone, this is my first time posting homebrew of any kind on this forum, and I wanted your opinions on my homebrew Lineage, the Stygians. For this lineage, I wanted to make something entirely alien in nature, both to humans and Prometheans.<br /> <br /> <b>Quick Summary</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Stygians possess an excess of the <b>Void</b> humour (in truth, this means that all their humours are dampened). This makes them erratic, inhuman, and perpetually hungry. They begin at <b>Humanity 5</b> instead of 7 to reflect this nature. They may only select <b>Centimanus</b> as their Refinement unless they have dots in the <b>Whispers of Humanity</b> merit (more dots opens up more refinements). Their Bewstowment, <b>Cthonic Void</b>, allows them to briefly ignore all need for air, as well as allowing them to ingest caustics for reduced damage. Their Mockery, <b>Death Stalkers</b>, hunt Prometheans with a method called <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persistence_hunting\" target=\"_blank\">persistence hunting</a>, chasing a Promethean from the edge of Azothic Radiance until it collapses of exhaustion.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The full writeup can be found at <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HYN6Hs3MKqQKidQACCHnNY8IJ_beWgyVQ507zCRLu5M/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">this google drive link here</a>. Please give me your feedback, and tell me what you think!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T17:49:02-07:00","id":458510,"title":"","content":"I think there's a really cool concept here, but the fact that you need to take a Merit (and spend XP raising Humanity) to follow a refinement other than Centimani makes them unplayable, so I can't see myself using them in a game.<br /> <br /> Additionally, from a writing standpoint, your Stereotypes need work-you can't just string together nonsense and expect it to look like madness. Madness isn't nonsense. Madness makes sense based on the supposition that something false is true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T18:18:32-07:00","id":458529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QuatreVingts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/457744-homebrew-stygian-lineage-void-filled-and-crazy?p=458510#post458510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, from a writing standpoint, your Stereotypes need work-you can't just string together nonsense and expect it to look like madness. Madness isn't nonsense. Madness makes sense based on the supposition that something false is true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I was probably going to think of something better for those later. But they are pretty lame in their current state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T15:31:13-07:00","id":467912,"title":"","content":"This seems like an antagonist Lineage, both functionally and thematically, and there's nothing wrong with that. I'd like to know more about the symbolism of the void in the context of abiogenesis, that is, how did the Demiurge access the void and come to see it as a potential source of animation? Also, I can see how being animated by absolute vacuum shapes the Torment and Wasteland, but I think Disquiet might work better if it was complementary instead of reflective. For example, the afflicted regard the Stygian as a consuming thief, so they begin to take pains to seal and protect themselves against his hunger. They plug up holes, duct tape plastic sheets over their windows, and freak out over drafts. They install additional locks, security cameras, and behave in a paranoid state about anything that isn't nailed down or secured in a vault. They feel like they can't breathe, become agoraphobic, and often end up suffocating themselves for having methodically sealed themselves away from the world a little too well, but at least the <i>thing</i> can't get in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T18:39:44-07:00","id":639683,"title":"","content":"i actually liked the stereotype a lot,but i think that'd be useful if you have a example character of the lineage in addition to the pandoran","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T19:41:22-07:00","id":639737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/457744-homebrew-stygian-lineage-void-filled-and-crazy?p=639683#post639683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i actually liked the stereotype a lot,but i think that'd be useful if you have a example character of the lineage in addition to the pandoran</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I was probably going to get to that, but as you can see, I never really did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-01T20:19:23-07:00","id":648539,"title":"","content":"While I find it to have tons of potential, currently these Stygians are not that appealing to be honest. They remind me of a fusion of Hollows and Zeky, but not as compelling. Now if theStygian was an Extempore, that would make it infinitely more appealing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}